WEBVTT

00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:19.780
Ah! My Goddess
Flights of Fancy

00:00:19.780 --> 00:00:23.310
Kono hiroi sekai no naka

00:00:24.620 --> 00:00:28.490
Deaubeki hitotachi ga

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:35.060
Mado no mukou niji no mukou ni mieru

00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:38.690
Kizuite iru hazu

00:00:40.870 --> 00:00:45.810
Kyuukutsu na omori o nuide

00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:48.780
Kimochi o yurushite

00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:56.090
Saa mimi o sumashi sono toki o matte

00:00:56.090 --> 00:00:58.850
Ima mezamenasai

00:01:00.020 --> 00:01:12.170
Oozora ni egaita chiisa na
yume o taisetsu ni shiyou

00:01:12.170 --> 00:01:19.410
Sou sureba itsumo shiawase ni nareru

00:01:19.410 --> 00:01:22.180
Kitto

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:26.550
Woh woh

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:42.260
Oh, my. These flowers...

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:48.100
That's right. That won't work for me now...

00:01:52.010 --> 00:01:53.800
They should be okay now!

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:56.170
Let's both do our best!

00:01:57.410 --> 00:02:01.520
Don't tell me Belldandy's had
her license suspended.

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:06.190
Poor Big Sister... I feel so bad for her
not being able to use magic!

00:02:06.190 --> 00:02:08.820
Belldandy can't even fly anymore?

00:02:09.190 --> 00:02:11.830
Well it IS only for a week, y'know.

00:02:11.830 --> 00:02:13.500
Huh? A week?

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:15.500
Yeah, a whole week!

00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:18.470
Even if they did say they'll
reissue her license,

00:02:18.470 --> 00:02:21.600
she's still gotta go back to Heaven
to take a refresher course!

00:02:22.070 --> 00:02:27.510
She'll have to watch a boring video and do this
magic simulator and stuff every single day.

00:02:27.510 --> 00:02:29.270
It is a total pain!

00:02:29.350 --> 00:02:32.780
But didn't you have to do it for
like 50 years or something?

00:02:32.780 --> 00:02:35.920
Yeah, but this is only her first time.
Feel better now?

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:38.650
Well... if it's just a week.

00:02:38.850 --> 00:02:40.390
Besides, she also...

00:02:40.390 --> 00:02:43.190
Oh! It's about time we were going to class.

00:02:43.890 --> 00:02:46.560
Today is Professor Kakuta's lecture, right?

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:48.500
Huh? Oh, uh, yeah...

00:02:49.030 --> 00:02:51.600
And she doesn't seem to be
the least bit down about it.

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:53.300
Oh, Big Sister...

00:02:55.170 --> 00:02:57.540
Oh, Morisato!

00:02:58.440 --> 00:03:04.380
Ah! It Doesn't Matter Where,
So Long As We're Together!

00:03:05.210 --> 00:03:08.050
Long time, no see, guys...

00:03:08.720 --> 00:03:10.880
We have a little favor to ask.

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:13.020
What's that?

00:03:13.020 --> 00:03:15.860
We want you to hang onto some
luggage for us, actually.

00:03:16.190 --> 00:03:19.220
Luggage? And how long do you
need me to hold onto it?

00:03:19.460 --> 00:03:21.590
One week.

00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:24.220
Okay, a week's fine.

00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:28.870
Hey, guys! He says it's okay!

00:03:28.870 --> 00:03:30.130
"Guys"?

00:03:43.020 --> 00:03:44.220
Oh, my.

00:03:44.220 --> 00:03:46.490
Sorry to trouble ya!
See, the dorm's being remodeled,

00:03:46.490 --> 00:03:48.790
and we were kind of in a pinch for
somewhere to store our stuff.

00:03:48.790 --> 00:03:51.780
Sorry for the little inconvenience,
but thanks for the help.

00:03:53.330 --> 00:03:56.070
Little? You call this little?

00:03:56.070 --> 00:03:57.770
Now, wait a minute, Keiichi!

00:03:57.770 --> 00:03:59.940
What are we supposed to do with this?!

00:03:59.940 --> 00:04:03.570
Hey, don't look at me!
None of you said anything!

00:04:03.570 --> 00:04:06.010
Tamiya's problems are your problems.

00:04:06.010 --> 00:04:08.180
Who decided that?!

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:10.270
I did just now.

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:12.710
Oh... Is that right?

00:04:13.250 --> 00:04:17.080
Well, I guess we can stick it in
the main temple if we have to.

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:20.260
Hey, sorry, Kei-chan!

00:04:20.260 --> 00:04:23.390
I just bought a new refrigerator,
washing machine, and kotatsu table,

00:04:23.390 --> 00:04:26.490
so could you store my old ones until
large item garbage collection?

00:04:29.160 --> 00:04:34.640
I got a these two rare bikes in good
condition for a steal at auction,

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:39.170
but I've got no space right now...
Once I've sorted out my garage,

00:04:39.170 --> 00:04:41.840
I'll come get them, so hang on to 'em
and these boxes, too, will ya?

00:04:44.410 --> 00:04:49.650
I bought too many clothes, and now
our storehouse is full to bursting.

00:04:49.650 --> 00:04:52.950
Would you mind hanging onto these until
we've completed the addition?

00:04:54.990 --> 00:04:56.050
Sure...

00:04:56.360 --> 00:05:00.300
You don't have to take
EVERYONE'S stuff, you know!

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:01.730
Yeah, but...

00:05:01.730 --> 00:05:03.170
I'm sorry.

00:05:03.170 --> 00:05:08.940
If I weren't under suspension,
I'd be able to shrink these things...

00:05:08.940 --> 00:05:10.910
Big Sister...

00:05:10.910 --> 00:05:13.370
It's all right! Leave it to me!

00:05:13.640 --> 00:05:15.340
Do you have some kind of plan?

00:05:15.340 --> 00:05:19.350
First, gather all the stuff in one place.
I'll tell you the rest then.

00:05:19.350 --> 00:05:22.480
Actually, that's a lot of trouble already.

00:05:47.510 --> 00:05:52.540
Okay, so here's the question:
Why can't we straighten this place up?

00:05:53.280 --> 00:05:55.080
Because there's no room?

00:05:55.080 --> 00:05:56.150
Correct!

00:05:56.150 --> 00:06:01.350
In other words...
the solution is to make space...

00:06:02.420 --> 00:06:04.890
Even the temple building is packed full, though.

00:06:04.890 --> 00:06:07.730
Mr. Morisato, are you listening?

00:06:08.230 --> 00:06:10.930
I said MAKE space.

00:06:10.930 --> 00:06:11.130
M-A-K-E!

00:06:11.130 --> 00:06:12.430
Make space
M-A-K-E!

00:06:13.140 --> 00:06:14.770
What the heck is this?!

00:06:14.770 --> 00:06:17.140
My "Space-Doubler." Here, check it out.

00:06:17.640 --> 00:06:21.780
Magnification mode: ON.
Increase the function area by six times...

00:06:21.780 --> 00:06:23.450
and confirm changes.

00:06:23.450 --> 00:06:24.570
START!

00:06:28.750 --> 00:06:30.850
What the heck happened?!

00:06:30.850 --> 00:06:32.550
The room got bigger!

00:06:32.550 --> 00:06:34.260
I made space.

00:06:34.260 --> 00:06:36.490
MADE space? How?

00:06:36.490 --> 00:06:39.160
Strictly speaking, I made
an "advance payment."

00:06:39.160 --> 00:06:43.930
One hour or two hours from now, this will
still be the same space, right?

00:06:43.930 --> 00:06:48.570
I've effectively increased the size of the present
space by sliding that future space into it!

00:06:48.570 --> 00:06:51.230
I don't really get it, but wow.

00:06:52.310 --> 00:06:55.340
Well, in any case we've got
ourselves some more room now.

00:06:55.340 --> 00:06:57.570
Okay, time for us to straighten up!

00:06:59.080 --> 00:07:01.680
They... ran off.

00:07:02.320 --> 00:07:05.750
Keiichi? I'll help you out.

00:07:05.750 --> 00:07:08.190
Thanks... I appreciate it!

00:07:13.060 --> 00:07:16.670
Well, I should be grateful I've at least
got somewhere to put the stuff.

00:07:16.670 --> 00:07:17.760
Keiichi!

00:07:18.870 --> 00:07:22.770
Where... should I put THIS?

00:07:23.110 --> 00:07:24.800
Whoa, you don't need to strain yourself!

00:07:24.910 --> 00:07:26.340
Photonic Force
Rice crackers

00:07:27.910 --> 00:07:29.070
Belldandy!

00:07:29.580 --> 00:07:31.810
My magic... No, I can't!

00:07:31.810 --> 00:07:35.440
If I use it during my suspension,
my license will be revoked!

00:07:41.420 --> 00:07:43.030
I'm sorry...

00:07:43.030 --> 00:07:44.490
It's okay.

00:07:50.400 --> 00:07:54.030
Well, now! I guess I'll put this over here!

00:07:54.800 --> 00:07:55.670
Damn!

00:07:57.170 --> 00:07:59.510
You're amazing, Keiichi.

00:07:59.510 --> 00:08:00.510
Huh?

00:08:00.510 --> 00:08:03.780
You think? I don't think
I'm anything special.

00:08:03.780 --> 00:08:09.840
Oh, no. I've become so powerless
just because I can't use magic.

00:08:10.290 --> 00:08:13.520
So compared to me, you ARE amazing.

00:08:14.790 --> 00:08:18.690
Well, let's just get as much as
we can done this morning.

00:08:19.500 --> 00:08:20.590
Sure!

00:08:21.830 --> 00:08:25.290
Except we're already running
out of space again, huh?

00:08:25.700 --> 00:08:28.000
How about we open up just a little more room?

00:08:28.700 --> 00:08:31.400
Oh, isn't that supposed to go this way?

00:08:31.670 --> 00:08:33.040
Was it?

00:08:33.880 --> 00:08:40.780
I think she said you select magnification
mode first, then the function area, right?

00:08:40.780 --> 00:08:43.480
Uh, which one is it? Umm...

00:08:43.750 --> 00:08:46.020
That should set it, and...

00:08:46.020 --> 00:08:48.260
Huh? Isn't that it?

00:08:48.260 --> 00:08:51.430
"Options"? Was there something like that?

00:08:51.430 --> 00:08:54.120
It is the right button after all, isn't it?

00:08:54.460 --> 00:08:55.630
See?

00:08:55.630 --> 00:08:56.970
You're right!

00:08:56.970 --> 00:09:00.800
Okay right, and now I put in the
value of the area ratio...

00:09:03.470 --> 00:09:05.700
Okay! How about that?

00:09:15.980 --> 00:09:20.280
Okay... I wonder if they're getting
the right mood on now?

00:09:22.120 --> 00:09:23.630
Huh? The whole room?!

00:09:23.630 --> 00:09:25.090
Big Sister!

00:09:35.300 --> 00:09:38.830
Belldandy! Keiichi!

00:09:39.340 --> 00:09:41.110
It's no use.

00:09:41.110 --> 00:09:44.310
It looks like it's been expanded
to almost infinite dimension.

00:09:44.610 --> 00:09:47.080
Your voice shouldn't be able to reach them.

00:09:47.350 --> 00:09:49.370
Infinite dimension?

00:09:53.660 --> 00:09:57.750
Where the heck... is the EXIT?!

00:10:01.330 --> 00:10:04.870
Don't tell me the "Space-Doubler"
has gone out of control!

00:10:04.870 --> 00:10:07.770
Hey... can't you reset that thing?

00:10:07.770 --> 00:10:10.040
Well, it's possible, but...

00:10:10.040 --> 00:10:14.840
you've gotta press UP, UP, DOWN, DOWN,
LEFT, RIGHT, LEFT, RIGHT

00:10:14.840 --> 00:10:16.850
and the "set" button twice!

00:10:16.850 --> 00:10:18.680
You think Keiichi could manage that?

00:10:18.680 --> 00:10:20.110
Probably not.

00:10:21.380 --> 00:10:24.450
No choice then... I'll hit reset.

00:10:24.450 --> 00:10:26.080
That won't work either.

00:10:26.460 --> 00:10:28.790
How the heck are you going to
get to where they are?

00:10:28.790 --> 00:10:32.890
Big Sister's forbidden from using magic
while she's under suspension.

00:10:33.260 --> 00:10:35.300
And since she can't use magic,

00:10:35.300 --> 00:10:38.760
we won't find any energy surges
to trace her by, is that it?

00:10:40.370 --> 00:10:42.640
If only we at least knew where she is...

00:10:42.640 --> 00:10:45.070
Well, it's not that we don't know...

00:10:45.070 --> 00:10:46.070
Huh?

00:10:46.070 --> 00:10:48.510
She's definitely in the center.

00:10:48.510 --> 00:10:51.610
Since the "Space-Doubler" expands space
outwards from where it is.

00:10:51.610 --> 00:10:54.250
Well that makes things easy, right?

00:10:54.250 --> 00:10:57.050
Yeah. Provided we know where the center IS.

00:10:57.050 --> 00:10:58.020
Huh?

00:10:58.820 --> 00:11:03.020
We won't be able to find the center
of this infinite dimension.

00:11:03.930 --> 00:11:06.830
What's more, this is emulated space.

00:11:06.830 --> 00:11:10.460
If you got lost in this, you'd never
find your way out again.

00:11:11.400 --> 00:11:15.200
Then we might as well not even know
where they are at all.

00:11:15.640 --> 00:11:17.610
Isn't there anything we can do?

00:11:30.790 --> 00:11:33.760
It's no use. We don't even know
which direction we're going.

00:11:36.190 --> 00:11:39.090
I guess there's no point walking
around aimlessly then.

00:11:39.090 --> 00:11:40.150
Yes.

00:11:41.230 --> 00:11:42.730
What is it?

00:11:42.730 --> 00:11:46.900
Well... I don't know if it's because you've
been suspended from using your magic,

00:11:46.900 --> 00:11:49.030
but you look kind of worn out.

00:11:49.740 --> 00:11:52.540
What about you? Are you all right?

00:11:52.770 --> 00:11:54.780
Oh, yeah, just fine!

00:11:54.780 --> 00:11:57.510
After all, I'm used to the upperclassmen
always putting me through the ringer!

00:11:57.510 --> 00:11:58.850
Oh, I guess so.

00:11:58.850 --> 00:12:01.480
Well, if this is how it is I guess
there's nothing we can do.

00:12:02.680 --> 00:12:06.420
We don't get too many chances
to just get it easy like this.

00:12:06.420 --> 00:12:08.690
Let's just take it easy and wait for
someone to come help us.

00:12:08.690 --> 00:12:10.160
Keiichi...

00:12:17.370 --> 00:12:19.330
It's quiet, isn't it?

00:12:19.570 --> 00:12:21.260
Amazingly quiet.

00:12:28.210 --> 00:12:30.050
Aren't you bored?

00:12:30.050 --> 00:12:35.880
No... I don't mind spending time like this,
not really doing anything.

00:12:36.220 --> 00:12:39.750
Actually, maybe I'm the one who's bored.

00:12:40.160 --> 00:12:43.280
Well, how about we do something
to pass the time then?

00:12:43.360 --> 00:12:49.600
Sure. Something just the two of us
can do, to distract ourselves...

00:12:49.600 --> 00:12:51.230
Sure.

00:12:52.100 --> 00:12:54.000
How does that thing get its power?

00:12:54.000 --> 00:12:55.170
Batteries.

00:12:55.170 --> 00:12:56.710
How long can they keep it running?

00:12:56.710 --> 00:12:58.140
One week.

00:12:58.140 --> 00:13:00.140
If we wait for the power to run out,

00:13:00.140 --> 00:13:03.180
even if Belldandy ends up okay,
Keiichi certainly won't last.

00:13:03.180 --> 00:13:05.580
I wouldn't be too worried about that.

00:13:05.580 --> 00:13:07.850
Keiichi will certainly be okay.

00:13:07.850 --> 00:13:09.150
Why do you say that?

00:13:09.150 --> 00:13:11.850
Well, because Big Sister is with him!

00:13:12.120 --> 00:13:13.520
Oh, right.

00:13:13.520 --> 00:13:17.260
Big Sister's suspension doesn't
mean she CAN'T use magic,

00:13:17.260 --> 00:13:19.260
she's just been banned temporarily.

00:13:19.260 --> 00:13:22.260
So if it ever did come down to it,
she could still use her magic.

00:13:22.260 --> 00:13:24.000
It's Belldandy we're talking about,

00:13:24.000 --> 00:13:27.330
so if Keiichi ever were in trouble,
I'm sure she would use it.

00:13:27.840 --> 00:13:31.670
Even if it meant losing her
qualification as a goddess.

00:13:31.670 --> 00:13:32.800
Yeah...

00:13:35.210 --> 00:13:37.550
Hmm... Food, huh?

00:13:37.550 --> 00:13:39.850
Lessee... Ooh, pasta!

00:13:39.850 --> 00:13:41.850
Note: They are playing a Japanese word game called shiritori.
"TA"? Um...

00:13:41.850 --> 00:13:44.120
The way it works is that you take the last syllable of
your opponents word and make another
word beginning with that syllable.
"TA"? Um...

00:13:44.120 --> 00:13:46.150
The reason this messes up the game is that the
Japanese letter N cannot begin any words.
Tamago-san (Mr. Egg).

00:13:46.150 --> 00:13:47.160
The reason this messes up the game is that the
Japanese letter N cannot begin any words.
You don't need to add the "-san" after it.

00:13:47.160 --> 00:13:49.620
You don't need to add the "-san" after it.

00:13:49.620 --> 00:13:50.790
I just...

00:13:50.790 --> 00:13:52.790
You add "-san" to just about
everything, you know.

00:13:52.790 --> 00:13:54.280
I'm sorry!

00:13:54.700 --> 00:13:58.270
Okay, let's try animals next, okay?

00:13:58.270 --> 00:13:59.330
Okay!

00:13:59.330 --> 00:14:01.370
Just remember to say their
names normally, okay?

00:14:01.370 --> 00:14:02.430
Okay!

00:14:04.340 --> 00:14:06.330
Have you come up with anything?

00:14:08.310 --> 00:14:13.440
Uh... hey! Can't you make a machine that will
advance time one week, but only here?

00:14:13.620 --> 00:14:16.620
Yeah, I can, but making it...

00:14:16.620 --> 00:14:19.450
would take six days.

00:14:20.820 --> 00:14:22.260
Not much use in it then.

00:14:22.260 --> 00:14:23.750
You said it...

00:14:25.290 --> 00:14:27.800
Does it hurt, Keiichi?

00:14:27.800 --> 00:14:29.460
I... I'm all right.

00:14:29.760 --> 00:14:32.290
I'm going to go a little deeper, okay?

00:14:32.770 --> 00:14:33.730
Sure.

00:14:34.100 --> 00:14:36.540
Now stay still for a bit.

00:14:37.710 --> 00:14:39.570
Okay, got it!

00:14:39.570 --> 00:14:41.580
Now for the other side.

00:14:41.580 --> 00:14:44.480
Uh... Okay...

00:14:46.280 --> 00:14:49.980
I wonder how long this dimension
will stay the way it is.

00:14:50.520 --> 00:14:53.320
I don't know if it'll be an hour or two, or...

00:14:53.590 --> 00:14:57.530
Well, I'm sure Skuld and Urd will
find a way to get us out!

00:14:57.530 --> 00:15:03.730
But, if we're stuck here like this
for a matter of days... you'll...

00:15:04.200 --> 00:15:09.200
I'll be fine. I've been out of money before
and gone a day or two without food.

00:15:09.200 --> 00:15:11.440
That much I can handle!

00:15:11.440 --> 00:15:14.770
But... I don't think I could.

00:15:15.280 --> 00:15:18.370
I couldn't stand to see you like that.

00:15:18.910 --> 00:15:20.610
Belldandy...

00:15:20.850 --> 00:15:24.550
I'm sure I'll end up using my magic!

00:15:25.290 --> 00:15:30.320
I'll save you, even if it means losing
my license as a goddess.

00:15:32.990 --> 00:15:35.430
Do you have so little trust in me?

00:15:35.430 --> 00:15:39.100
I'd like you to have a little more
faith in me in times like this.

00:15:39.100 --> 00:15:40.440
What do you mean?

00:15:40.440 --> 00:15:42.940
We can't let ourselves get discouraged!

00:15:42.940 --> 00:15:44.770
I know someone will come to help us.

00:15:44.770 --> 00:15:48.540
As long as we believe, then
the door will open for us.

00:15:50.950 --> 00:15:54.150
You're really amazing, Keiichi.

00:15:54.150 --> 00:15:55.140
Huh?

00:15:55.480 --> 00:15:57.850
I felt so anxious.

00:15:58.990 --> 00:16:01.720
Until now, I've wanted to get closer to you,

00:16:01.720 --> 00:16:05.160
and I've avoided using magic
if at all possible...

00:16:05.160 --> 00:16:07.900
I wouldn't even have cared if I had
lost the ability altogether.

00:16:07.900 --> 00:16:09.760
Or so I thought, at least.

00:16:09.760 --> 00:16:11.030
Belldandy...

00:16:11.270 --> 00:16:15.900
But, now it's like I've been
stripped of something...

00:16:15.900 --> 00:16:18.540
Now I've been banned from using my power,

00:16:18.540 --> 00:16:22.640
and I'm learning about YOUR
strength all over again.

00:16:22.640 --> 00:16:25.410
And my own weakness as well...

00:16:25.410 --> 00:16:26.710
I'm sorry.

00:16:27.020 --> 00:16:30.890
I figured we'd manage fine for just a week,

00:16:30.890 --> 00:16:35.380
but I didn't consider how tough it is
for you to be without your magic.

00:16:36.490 --> 00:16:39.720
I can remain like I am now without changing...

00:16:40.300 --> 00:16:45.530
I may not ever be able to truly
understand your pain.

00:16:45.530 --> 00:16:46.860
Keiichi...

00:16:47.270 --> 00:16:51.310
So I can't simply comfort you
like it's no sweat,

00:16:51.310 --> 00:16:53.870
but I can at least say I'm with you!

00:16:55.810 --> 00:16:59.010
Well, I am pretty powerless, though...

00:16:59.010 --> 00:17:02.210
Oh, no! You're couldn't be
any more encouraging!

00:17:10.960 --> 00:17:13.020
B-B-B-Belldandy!

00:17:13.560 --> 00:17:14.960
Let's dance!

00:17:16.260 --> 00:17:20.340
Say, why not make two machines that
can advance time by three days each?

00:17:20.340 --> 00:17:24.270
I can make one of those in a couple days,
so it'd be four days altogether!

00:17:24.270 --> 00:17:26.900
Keiichi can deal with the hunger until then!

00:17:27.240 --> 00:17:31.450
But Big Sister wouldn't be able to
handle seeing him like that.

00:17:31.450 --> 00:17:33.070
You're right...

00:17:36.350 --> 00:17:39.650
I can't use magic, but this
much I can manage.

00:17:40.090 --> 00:17:45.360
Hey, we danced like this one time when we
were competing with Sayoko, didn't we, right?

00:17:45.360 --> 00:17:49.320
I wasn't able to dance very well back then.

00:17:50.200 --> 00:17:51.700
You know, this kind of reminds me

00:17:51.700 --> 00:17:54.670
of the "folk dance" we used to do during
our field days back in school.

00:17:55.200 --> 00:17:56.910
Is that fun?

00:17:56.910 --> 00:17:58.370
Yeah.

00:17:59.640 --> 00:18:02.240
Hang on just a little longer, Lysander.

00:18:03.810 --> 00:18:05.410
Hello!

00:18:05.410 --> 00:18:09.680
I accidentally put this kitty's food in with
the packages I gave you earlier,

00:18:09.680 --> 00:18:11.950
and I was hoping to take that
back now, if you don't mind.

00:18:11.950 --> 00:18:14.890
This really isn't a good time for that now.

00:18:15.720 --> 00:18:17.890
So where is my stuff?

00:18:17.890 --> 00:18:20.700
Maybe if I asked Morisato
or Bell they'd know...

00:18:20.700 --> 00:18:22.790
I'm telling you now's not the time for...

00:18:24.070 --> 00:18:26.500
Hey! Morisato!

00:18:26.870 --> 00:18:27.670
The founder of the Auto Club's here!

00:18:27.670 --> 00:18:29.040
Now wait a darn minute!
The founder of the Auto Club's here!

00:18:29.040 --> 00:18:29.730
Now wait a darn minute!

00:18:29.940 --> 00:18:32.740
Hey, where are Morisato and Bell?

00:18:33.910 --> 00:18:38.210
WE'RE TELLING YOU THAT NOW IS NOT A
GOOD TIME FOR THIS, ALL RIGHT?!

00:18:39.010 --> 00:18:40.140
Lysander!

00:18:41.550 --> 00:18:46.320
Master Keiichi, your bath is ready, sir.
The water is just right.

00:18:46.320 --> 00:18:48.850
Good. Well, I guess I'll go on in.

00:18:49.120 --> 00:18:51.560
Shall I wash your back for you?

00:18:51.560 --> 00:18:54.460
More importantly, is dinner ready?

00:18:54.460 --> 00:18:56.600
It is being prepared as we speak, sir.

00:18:56.600 --> 00:18:59.530
Then come once you have finished with that.

00:18:59.530 --> 00:19:01.160
Very good, sir.

00:19:01.300 --> 00:19:02.200
Splish splash splish...

00:19:02.200 --> 00:19:02.840
"Oh, fishy fish, oh, fishy fish,
herring and bonito and tuna..."
Splish splash splish...

00:19:02.840 --> 00:19:05.540
"Oh, fishy fish, oh, fishy fish,
herring and bonito and tuna..."

00:19:05.540 --> 00:19:07.540
"Oh, fishy fish, oh, fishy fish,
herring and bonito and tuna..."
Ah, it feels great!

00:19:07.540 --> 00:19:08.600
"Oh, fishy fish, oh, fishy fish,
herring and bonito and tuna..."

00:19:09.040 --> 00:19:11.850
I shall wash your back now, sir.

00:19:11.850 --> 00:19:14.370
Ahh, this is heaven!

00:19:14.950 --> 00:19:19.550
Tonight's main course is a
Scandinavian delicacy, surstromming.

00:19:19.550 --> 00:19:22.890
Wow, it smells great! I appreciate the meal!

00:19:24.330 --> 00:19:26.320
Delicious! This is splendid!

00:19:26.560 --> 00:19:28.430
It is an honor to hear that.

00:19:28.430 --> 00:19:30.530
Ah, yes! Will you have some, too?

00:19:30.530 --> 00:19:32.530
It would be wasted on me, sir.

00:19:32.530 --> 00:19:34.830
Don't be so reserved. Now come closer!

00:19:35.570 --> 00:19:37.970
If you won't, then I will!

00:19:45.180 --> 00:19:47.020
Ah, I'm such an idiot!

00:19:47.020 --> 00:19:48.020
I'm sorry!
Ah, I'm such an idiot!

00:19:48.020 --> 00:19:48.480
I'm sorry!

00:19:48.480 --> 00:19:52.790
Did our pretending make you
even hungrier instead?

00:19:52.790 --> 00:19:55.690
No, that's not the problem...

00:19:55.690 --> 00:19:56.750
Huh?

00:19:57.690 --> 00:19:59.890
Infinite space above and around...

00:19:59.890 --> 00:20:02.830
On the other hand, the floor
feels like this...

00:20:03.400 --> 00:20:07.840
I've got it! This infinite space
isn't "infinitely" DEEP!

00:20:08.700 --> 00:20:12.270
In other words, everything
BENEATH us might be like normal!

00:20:12.270 --> 00:20:14.710
All right! Now we're going somewhere!

00:20:14.710 --> 00:20:15.980
Please wait a moment!

00:20:15.980 --> 00:20:16.980
Huh?

00:20:16.980 --> 00:20:19.040
What if you're wrong?

00:20:20.050 --> 00:20:22.520
If we make a tear in this dimension,

00:20:23.550 --> 00:20:26.180
it might go through to another world!

00:20:27.690 --> 00:20:29.320
That's...

00:20:32.690 --> 00:20:33.990
Let's open it up.

00:20:34.430 --> 00:20:39.660
I'd rather fall into an unknown world than
be stuck in this infinite dimension.

00:20:40.740 --> 00:20:42.200
I guess you're right.

00:20:42.570 --> 00:20:45.270
Besides, no matter where we go,

00:20:45.270 --> 00:20:47.570
as long as I've got you with me...
as long as I've got you with me...

00:21:07.130 --> 00:21:09.260
One, and a two, and a... THREE!

00:21:12.170 --> 00:21:13.230
Huh?

00:21:13.230 --> 00:21:15.200
Waugh, it IS another world!

00:21:19.970 --> 00:21:21.270
You did it!

00:21:21.640 --> 00:21:25.010
Lysander! Where'd you go?!

00:21:26.050 --> 00:21:27.620
Lysander!

00:21:27.620 --> 00:21:29.820
Oh, thank goodness you're all right!

00:21:29.820 --> 00:21:32.090
Well, it looks like Morisato's not around,

00:21:32.090 --> 00:21:34.880
so I guess for today you'll just have to
put up with the other cat food I bought.

00:21:36.620 --> 00:21:39.360
Huh? Is that Chihiro on the way out?

00:21:39.360 --> 00:21:42.760
That cat must be hers.

00:21:43.300 --> 00:21:45.900
What if you make six machines that
shorten time by a day each?

00:21:45.900 --> 00:21:48.540
I could make one of those in half a day, so...

00:21:48.540 --> 00:21:50.810
Awesome! I'd be done in three days!

00:21:50.810 --> 00:21:54.170
Oh, sheesh... You know, I think
it's peaceful enough out here.

00:21:54.480 --> 00:21:59.350
Keiichi, I guess I do want to
keep being a goddess.

00:21:59.350 --> 00:22:03.820
I'll have to bear being without
magic for a week, but...

00:22:03.820 --> 00:22:10.660
would it be all right if I still stay with you,
even if I can't use my powers?

00:22:10.890 --> 00:22:13.490
Well, of course it's all right! Obviously!

00:22:15.730 --> 00:22:17.700
But... Keiichi?

00:22:17.930 --> 00:22:19.170
Huh?

00:22:19.170 --> 00:22:21.800
Being human is great, too.

00:22:30.110 --> 00:22:34.880
Ichinichi oeru tabi

00:22:34.880 --> 00:22:47.860
"Kyou mo anata no koto daisuki deshita" to
sotto mune ni omou

00:22:47.860 --> 00:22:52.000
Omoikaeseba hora

00:22:52.000 --> 00:22:57.370
Nakitsukareta hi mo atta keredo

00:22:57.370 --> 00:23:06.210
Sonna yoru o ikutsu mo koete
tadoritsuita basho

00:23:06.210 --> 00:23:10.620
Soshite maku aketa story

00:23:10.620 --> 00:23:16.920
Nandaka yume mitai na real

00:23:16.920 --> 00:23:25.200
Sukoshi terewarainagara mo tsunaida te wa

00:23:25.200 --> 00:23:35.780
Kitto kazoekirenu hodo no
ai no yokan ga afuredashite iru

00:23:35.780 --> 00:23:45.250
Datte magire mo naku hoka de
mo nai anata to atashi wa

00:23:45.250 --> 00:23:50.280
Koibito doushi na no

00:23:55.900 --> 00:23:59.300
My goddess powers cause
Keiichi misfortune...

00:23:59.300 --> 00:24:03.470
What can I do for her during her greatest test?

00:24:03.470 --> 00:24:04.740
Next time: "Ah! Would It Be Okay
If I Were A Demon?!"

00:24:04.740 --> 00:24:07.140
Ah! Would It Be Okay If I Were A Demon?!
Next time: "Ah! Would It Be Okay
If I Were A Demon?!"

00:24:07.140 --> 00:24:09.670
Ah! Would It Be Okay If I Were A Demon?!
Even if you weren't a goddess...
